<script class="sapp-init" type="application/json" id="sapp-config">
{
  "license": {
    "host": {{ shop.permanent_domain | json }},
    "token": {{ sapp_license_token | json }},
    "expiresAt": {{ sapp_license_expires }}
  },
  "debug": false,
  {%- comment -%}
    INP schedule: the original timeouts + paced queues (queueOptions) + one
    Airwallex rule, no per-vendor rules. Earlier timeouts did not change INP in
    isolated tests; they only start analytics sooner.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "timeouts": {
    "mobile":  { "preload": "1000", "scripts": "3500", "embeds": "4500", "other": "1000", "async": "5500" },
    "desktop": { "preload": "500", "scripts": "3500", "embeds": "4500", "other": "1000", "async": "5500" }
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    OPTIONAL slow-connection profile. The backend selects it at start time when
    the measured network is slow (window.__sapp.net.slow — from the LCP/document
    throughput probe), or when forced via ?sappconn=slow. Omit the block to always
    use `timeouts`. Here the heavy queues are pushed far back so on a weak link
    the pipe and main thread stay clear during the early-interaction window
    (e.g. add-to-cart, which is LCP-lane and unaffected); set a queue to "none"
    to skip it entirely for slow users. Must differ from `timeouts` to matter.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  "timeoutsSlow": {
    "mobile":  { "preload": "2500", "scripts": "6000", "embeds": "10000", "other": "3000", "async": "12000" },
    "desktop": { "preload": "2000", "scripts": "6000", "embeds": "10000", "other": "3000", "async": "12000" }
  },
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    "*" applies to every queue (a per-queue key overrides it). stagger trickles a
    queue's scripts one-by-one with a fixed gap instead of firing the whole batch
    at once — fewer simultaneous downloads (bandwidth stays free for user actions
    like add-to-cart) and spread-out execution (main thread stays responsive).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    One external script per chunk with a gap, and inline work cut into 15 ms
    slices, so the thread keeps short idle gaps where a tap is handled at once.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "queueOptions": {
    "*":       { "stagger": 90, "burst": 1, "slice": 15 },
    "scripts": { "stagger": 90, "burst": 1, "slice": 15 },
    "embeds":  { "stagger": 150, "burst": 1, "slice": 15 },
    "async":   { "stagger": 150, "burst": 1, "slice": 15 }
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    OPTIONAL gentler pacing for slow connections — selected at queue-run time by
    the same trigger as timeoutsSlow (measured window.__sapp.net.slow, or forced
    via ?sappconn=slow). Slow link ≈ narrow pipe + weak CPU, so: smaller burst
    (fewer simultaneous downloads), larger stagger (more breathing room), smaller
    slice (yield to input sooner). Omit this block to use `queueOptions` always.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  "queueOptionsSlow": {
    "*":       { "stagger": 100, "burst": 3, "slice": 12 },
    "scripts": { "stagger": 100, "burst": 1, "slice": 12 },
    "async":   { "stagger": 200, "burst": 1, "slice": 12 }
  },
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "dispatchSyntheticEvents": true,
  "defaultMediaTrigger": "scroll",
  "rules": [
    { 
      "match": { "innerHTML": "ShopifyAnalytics" },
      "queue": "loaded",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    { 
      "match": { "innerHTML": "gtm.js" },
      "queue": "preload",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    { 
      "match": { "id": "web-pixels-manager-setup" },
      "queue": "other",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    {%- comment -%} Triggers are scroll/touchstart only — NO `click`/`mousemove` — so the add-to-cart
      click (and desktop hover) never wakes these heavier third parties on the cart interaction. The
      reviews widget (widget.min.js) is additionally kicked by the rating-anchor fix in __sapp-custom.js
      on a rating click, since there is no `click` trigger to load it for that flow. {%- endcomment -%}
    {
      "match": { "src": "portable-wallets" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "touchstart"]
    },
    {
      "match": { "src": "E-v1.js" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "touchstart"]
    },
    {
      "match": { "src": "player.js" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "touchstart"]
    },
    {
      "match": { "src": "widget.min.js" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "touchstart"]
    },
    {%- comment -%} Airwallex fraud protection draws nothing on the storefront but is one of the
      heaviest scripts; it only fingerprints the device for orders (Klarna/Afterpay go through
      Airwallex). n-airwallex-on-cart runs it when the slide cart opens or on the /cart page. {%- endcomment -%}
    {
      "match": { "src": "airwallex-fraud-protection" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["manual"]
    },
    {%- comment -%} BookEasy only serves the "Book a call" consultation (a service with no products), so
      its widget, and the reCAPTCHA it pulls in, load only when that link is clicked: n-book-easy runs
      these tasks. The app embed's inline cart validation does not need the widget and stays as is. {%- endcomment -%}
    {
      "match": { "src": "bookeasy-widget" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": "manual"
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": {
    "id":        ["sapp-config"],
    "class":     ["sapp-init", "__init"],
    "innerHTML": {{ sapp_init_innerhtml | json }},
    "src":       {{ sapp_init_src | json }}
  }
}
</script>